0.2.0
-----
== Upgrading from 0.1.0
`ALTER EXTENSION object_reference UPDATE` migrates an existing 0.1.0 install.
The `reg*` pseudotype columns on `_object_reference._object_oid` are replaced
by plain `oid` columns (see below), so anything that read those internal
columns directly must switch to `objid`/`classid`.

== Remove the `count_nulls` dependency
The `reg*` pseudotype columns (`regclass`, `regconfig`, `regdictionary`,
`regnamespace`, `regoperator`, `regprocedure`, `regtype`) on
`_object_reference._object_oid` are gone, replaced by plain `oid` `classid`
and `objid` columns. That removes the only use of `count_nulls`, so it is no
longer required.

== Add `object__describe()`, `object__identity()` and `object__cleanup()`
`object__describe()` and `object__identity()` wrap `pg_describe_object()` and
`pg_identify_object()`. `object__cleanup()` deletes an object's reference
if nothing else still uses it, ignoring `foreign_key_violation`. It now runs
automatically when an object is removed from its last object group.

== Refuse to track temporary objects
`object__getsert()` raises an error for objects in a `pg_temp*` or
`pg_toast_temp*` schema.

== Refuse to track object_reference's own objects
`object__getsert()` raises `feature_not_supported` for any member of the
object_reference extension itself.

== Support cat_tools 0.3.0
Adapted to cat_tools 0.3.0's renamed `routine__parse_arg_types_text()`.
Partitioned tables and partitioned indexes are listed as unsupported object
types (`object_reference.unsupported()`), because `pg_get_object_address()`
can't round-trip them.

== Stop overriding `client_min_messages` during install
`CREATE EXTENSION` already raises it as needed; the script's own setting
could lower a stricter caller's level.
